<%# Sales Tax result (spec issue #252, DESIGN.md §4) — composes BLEND components:
      • Hero-result — the figure the chosen mode SOLVED FOR (the unknown answer to the question
                      asked): the after-tax price, before-tax price, or tax rate. 5px coral left
                      rule, big tabular-nums, with a one-line detail naming the tax amount.
      • Stat grid   — all four figures (before-tax price, tax amount, after-tax price, tax rate)
                      from the shared `.stat-grid` / `.stat-card` component (issue #143), on the
                      `--wide` track: the worst-case money runs high-magnitude (7-figure money
                      like $1,000,000.00) which the default 9.5rem track would wrap mid-number in
                      the narrow result panel. The tax amount reads in accent (the focal computed
                      figure, DESIGN.md §1).
      • Data table  — the bill-style breakdown (before-tax price + tax = after-tax price), thin
                      rule borders, right-aligned tabular-nums, a hard ink total row.
    The backend owns every number (ARCHITECTURE.md §4); this only renders the envelope's values
    (before_tax_price / after_tax_price / rate / tax_amount). `calc:` is a valid
    Calculators::SalesTax — the empty + error states are handled one level up in _result.html.erb.
    Structural twin of VAT (#255) — keep the result layout parallel. %>
<% r = calc.result %>
<% hero = sales_tax_hero(calc) %>
<div class="space-y-6">
  <%# ── Hero: the solved-for figure (DESIGN.md §4 "Hero-result") ─────────────────
      The headline answer is the figure the mode solved for. 5px coral left rule + big
      tabular-nums; the detail line states the tax amount on the price. %>
  <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
    <div class="flex gap-5 p-7">
      <span class="w-[5px] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="min-w-0">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent"><%= hero[:eyebrow] %></p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.04em] tabular-nums text-ink">
          <%= hero[:value] %>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          At a <span class="font-semibold text-ink"><%= sales_tax_rate_display(r[:rate]) %>%</span> rate,
          the tax is
          <span class="font-semibold text-accent">$<%= money_display(r[:tax_amount]) %></span>
          on a <span class="font-semibold text-ink">$<%= money_display(r[:before_tax_price]) %></span>
          before-tax price.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# ── Stat grid: the four figures (DESIGN.md §4 "Stat grid", #143) ─────────────
      The shared responsive stat grid on the `--wide` track (13rem min) — the worst-case money
      values run high-magnitude (7-figure), which the default 9.5rem track would wrap mid-number
      in the narrow (~489px) panel; the `.stat-card` never-clip net (overflow-wrap on the value
      `<dd>`) catches any larger worst case. This grid sits directly on the page background (a
      top-level block, not nested in a surface card), so the cards use `.stat-card--surface` to
      stand off the cream. Tax amount reads in accent (the focal computed figure, DESIGN.md §1). %>
  <dl class="stat-grid stat-grid--wide">
    <div class="stat-card stat-card--surface">
      <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Before-tax price</dt>
      <dd class="mt-1.5 break-words text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] tabular-nums text-ink">$<%= money_display(r[:before_tax_price]) %></dd>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-card stat-card--surface">
      <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Tax amount</dt>
      <dd class="mt-1.5 break-words text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] tabular-nums text-accent">$<%= money_display(r[:tax_amount]) %></dd>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-card stat-card--surface">
      <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">After-tax price</dt>
      <dd class="mt-1.5 break-words text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] tabular-nums text-ink">$<%= money_display(r[:after_tax_price]) %></dd>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-card stat-card--surface">
      <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Tax rate</dt>
      <dd class="mt-1.5 break-words text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] tabular-nums text-ink"><%= sales_tax_rate_display(r[:rate]) %>%</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <%# ── Breakdown (DESIGN.md §4 "Data table") ────────────────────────────────────
      before-tax price + tax = after-tax price. Thin rule borders, right-aligned tabular-nums, a
      hard ink total row. The tax line reads in accent (the amount added). %>
  <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
    <div class="p-7">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">Breakdown</p>
      <table class="mt-4 w-full text-[15px]">
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-rule">
            <th scope="row" class="py-2 text-left font-medium text-muted">Before-tax price</th>
            <td class="py-2 text-right tabular-nums text-ink">$<%= money_display(r[:before_tax_price]) %></td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-rule">
            <th scope="row" class="py-2 text-left font-medium text-muted">Sales tax (<%= sales_tax_rate_display(r[:rate]) %>%)</th>
            <td class="py-2 text-right tabular-nums text-accent">+&nbsp;$<%= money_display(r[:tax_amount]) %></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" class="border-t-2 border-ink py-2 text-left font-bold text-ink">After-tax price</th>
            <td class="border-t-2 border-ink py-2 text-right font-bold tabular-nums text-ink">$<%= money_display(r[:after_tax_price]) %></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
